{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0195fLfhsM9THWB3DsPLWdud","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-553\"\n3\ttitle = \"The hold ban mechanized: claim-ref check, blocked_pending retired, fragment declaration cross-checked (OI-70)\"\n4\tspecref = \"\"\n5\tworkstream = \"process\"\n6\tsr_refs = []\n7\tneeds = []\n8\tbuildtier = \"medium\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n10\tpriority = 3\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Deliverable\n14\t\n15\tOI-70's hold-by-rename ban mechanized, all four Done-when arms shipped:\n16\t\n17\t1. **Claim-ref check** — `check_trajectory.holdbyrename_findings` reports every\n18\t   `docs/work/active/<branch>/` claim directory with no matching\n19\t   `refs/heads/<branch>` (the rename-hold / phantom-head signature). Warn at the\n20\t   commit bar, ERROR under `--strict` (the DevStg-Impl gate), silent off-git —\n21\t   the R-E/R-F promotable tier, no new `main()` branch. `tests/test_trajectory_holdban.py`\n22\t   drives it both ways on a git scaffold plus the empty-dir and off-git edges;\n23\t   tiered into `conftest.SLOW_MODULES`.\n24\t2. **`blockref` vocabulary retired** — `pending.blocked_pending` (the owner\n25\t   surface with zero producers) and the `blockref` FIELD are gone: both loaders,\n26\t   the canonical `kitlib.registry.WI_COLUMNS`, `wi_convert`, `plan_artifacts`,\n27\t   the shipped template header, and the three derivations (`schedule._disposition`'s\n28\t   blocked arm, `traj_views._wi_status`, `blocked_pending`). The `-000` example\n29\t   twin, README twins, authored docs, and a RESYNC_PACK.md entry follow. The\n30\t   `blocked` WI-384 status WORD stays as defensive vocabulary (OI-70 retires the\n31\t   mechanism, not the status model); the `Blocked-WI:`/`BlockRef:` COMMIT\n32\t   TRAILERS (a worker's block signal) are a distinct, live instrument, untouched.\n33\t3. **Fragment `none` cross-checked** — `gen_open_items` ARM 4\n34\t   (`_none_declaration_findings` + `_scope_span`): a fragment declaring\n35\t   `Deferred open items: none` while its own scope cites a PENDING open item is\n36\t   contradicted, the TRUTH check beside ARM 2's presence check. Position-is-scope,\n37\t   warn-first, fail-soft. Four tests.\n38\t4. **Ban stated where supervisors read** — the session-protocol skill (a\n39\t   Standing rule), `docs/handbacks/README.md`, and the ADJUDICATE\n40\t   `adjudicate-disposition` prompt name the partial close as the ONLY sanctioned\n41\t   stop and cite OI-70.\n42\t\n43\tRatchets re-stamped for the change (`check_trajectory` SLOC 2245→2273,\n44\t`stack.ini` smoke `max-tests` →1467, the `gen_open_items` newline-site pin);\n45\t`PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` +43 flagged in the byte-budget-guard skill; skill copies +\n46\t`prompts/CATALOG.md` regenerated. Full unfiltered suite: 3219 passed; the only\n47\tfailures are a pre-existing ruff-0.16.5 skew (I001 in the bootstrap-generated\n48\tdemo) confirmed identical on the integration base, unrelated to this WI.\n49\tFOLLOW-UP surfaced, not fixed (out of lane, `sr_refs = []`): five Approved spine\n50\tcells (LLR-158/161/198, two TC Methods) still *describe* the retired blockref\n51\tmechanism — semantic prose drift only (no snapshot drift, no re-attest triggered,\n52\tno new crosscheck finding), left for a spine-hygiene pass / owner re-attest.\n53\t\n54\t## Context\n55\t\n56\t`OI-70`'s ruling bans the hold-by-rename outright — a lane must close or it\n57\tgets lost, as the wi508 lane nearly was — and the owner endorsed the\n58\tmechanization: a claim directory must have a matching branch ref. That\n59\tmismatch (spec in `active/`, no ref) is the rename-hold's exact signature and\n60\tthe same scheduler/dispatcher disagreement `docs/handoff-2026-08-31.md` §2\n61\tnames as the phantom head. Two dead surfaces ride with the ruling:\n62\t`pending.blocked_pending` reads `queued/` rows carrying a `blockref` and\n63\tNOTHING produces one any more (`LLR-161` removed the producers), and\n64\t`gen_open_items.py --check` verifies a fragment DECLARES its deferred open\n65\titems without checking the declaration is true.\n66\t\n67\t## Done-when\n68\t\n69\t1. A check (harness-run, warn-or-gate per the declared policy) reports every\n70\t   `docs/work/active/<branch>/` claim directory with no matching branch ref —\n71\t   driven on a scaffold both ways (matching ref: silent; renamed ref: named).\n72\t2. `pending.blocked_pending` and the `blockref` vocabulary are retired or\n73\t   re-pointed — the owner surface keeps no source with zero producers; the\n74\t   `-000` example row and any doc teaching `blockref` follow in the same\n75\t   slice.\n76\t3. The fragment deferred-open-items declaration is cross-checked against the\n77\t   registry (a fragment claiming `none` while it should have deferred a row\n78\t   is contradicted), not merely presence-checked.\n79\t4. The ban is stated where supervisors read: the session-protocol skill and\n80\t   the handback/ADJUDICATE docs name the sanctioned stop (the partial close;\n81\t   nothing else) and cite `OI-70` as the ruling of record.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2b0eee3-07f3-4ea6-8f78-0c8300a24eee","uuid":"010c09d4-7cfd-4669-bdee-7ed534fc40ee","timestamp":"2026-09-01T11:17:26.044Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-553-hold-ban-and-surface-hygiene/docs/archive/work/complete/WI-553-hold-ban-and-surface-hygiene.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-553\"\ntitle = \"The hold ban mechanized: claim-ref check, blocked_pending retired, fragment declaration cross-checked (OI-70)\"\nspecref = \"\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nsr_refs = []\nneeds = []\nbuildtier = \"medium\"\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\npriority = 3\n+++\n\n## Deliverable\n\nOI-70's hold-by-rename ban mechanized, all four Done-when arms shipped:\n\n1. **Claim-ref check** — `check_trajectory.holdbyrename_findings` reports every\n   `docs/work/active/<branch>/` claim directory with no matching\n   `refs/heads/<branch>` (the rename-hold / phantom-head signature). Warn at the\n   commit bar, ERROR under `--strict` (the DevStg-Impl gate), silent off-git —\n   the R-E/R-F promotable tier, no new `main()` branch. `tests/test_trajectory_holdban.py`\n   drives it both ways on a git scaffold plus the empty-dir and off-git edges;\n   tiered into `conftest.SLOW_MODULES`.\n2. **`blockref` vocabulary retired** — `pending.blocked_pending` (the owner\n   surface with zero producers) and the `blockref` FIELD are gone: both loaders,\n   the canonical `kitlib.registry.WI_COLUMNS`, `wi_convert`, `plan_artifacts`,\n   the shipped template header, and the three derivations (`schedule._disposition`'s\n   blocked arm, `traj_views._wi_status`, `blocked_pending`). The `-000` example\n   twin, README twins, authored docs, and a RESYNC_PACK.md entry follow. The\n   `blocked` WI-384 status WORD stays as defensive vocabulary (OI-70 retires the\n   mechanism, not the status model); the `Blocked-WI:`/`BlockRef:` COMMIT\n   TRAILERS (a worker's block signal) are a distinct, live instrument, untouched.\n3. **Fragment `none` cross-checked** — `gen_open_items` ARM 4\n   (`_none_declaration_findings` + `_scope_span`): a fragment declaring\n   `Deferred open items: none` while its own scope cites a PENDING open item is\n   contradicted, the TRUTH check beside ARM 2's presence check. Position-is-scope,\n   warn-first, fail-soft. Four tests.\n4. **Ban stated where supervisors read** — the session-protocol skill (a\n   Standing rule), `docs/handbacks/README.md`, and the ADJUDICATE\n   `adjudicate-disposition` prompt name the partial close as the ONLY sanctioned\n   stop and cite OI-70.\n\nRatchets re-stamped for the change (`check_trajectory` SLOC 2245→2273,\n`stack.ini` smoke `max-tests` →1467, the `gen_open_items` newline-site pin);\n`PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` +43 flagged in the byte-budget-guard skill; skill copies +\n`prompts/CATALOG.md` regenerated. Full unfiltered suite: 3219 passed; the only\nfailures are a pre-existing ruff-0.16.5 skew (I001 in the bootstrap-generated\ndemo) confirmed identical on the integration base, unrelated to this WI.\nFOLLOW-UP surfaced, not fixed (out of lane, `sr_refs = []`): five Approved spine\ncells (LLR-158/161/198, two TC Methods) still *describe* the retired blockref\nmechanism — semantic prose drift only (no snapshot drift, no re-attest triggered,\nno new crosscheck finding), left for a spine-hygiene pass / owner re-attest.\n\n## Context\n\n`OI-70`'s ruling bans the hold-by-rename outright — a lane must close or it\ngets lost, as the wi508 lane nearly was — and the owner endorsed the\nmechanization: a claim directory must have a matching branch ref. That\nmismatch (spec in `active/`, no ref) is the rename-hold's exact signature and\nthe same scheduler/dispatcher disagreement `docs/handoff-2026-08-31.md` §2\nnames as the phantom head. Two dead surfaces ride with the ruling:\n`pending.blocked_pending` reads `queued/` rows carrying a `blockref` and\nNOTHING produces one any more (`LLR-161` removed the producers), and\n`gen_open_items.py --check` verifies a fragment DECLARES its deferred open\nitems without checking the declaration is true.\n\n## Done-when\n\n1. A check (harness-run, warn-or-gate per the declared policy) reports every\n   `docs/work/active/<branch>/` claim directory with no matching branch ref —\n   driven on a scaffold both ways (matching ref: silent; renamed ref: named).\n2. `pending.blocked_pending` and the `blockref` vocabulary are retired or\n   re-pointed — the owner surface keeps no source with zero producers; the\n   `-000` example row and any doc teaching `blockref` follow in the same\n   slice.\n3. The fragment deferred-open-items declaration is cross-checked against the\n   registry (a fragment claiming `none` while it should have deferred a row\n   is contradicted), not merely presence-checked.\n4. The ban is stated where supervisors read: the session-protocol skill and\n   the handback/ADJUDICATE docs name the sanctioned stop (the partial close;\n   nothing else) and cite `OI-70` as the ruling of record.\n","numLines":82,"startLine":1,"totalLines":82}}}
