{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CecfcTVPYAQwrAtFG3go1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JVgfQ78itKQKAY6c32wNrx","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/repointing-approved-spine-during-rework.md","content":"---\nname: repointing-approved-spine-during-rework\ndescription: When a WI deletes a mechanism, re-point its Approved spine cells in-lane (don't defer) and complete the IF-seam consequence; never leave WI/OI citations in the cell\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nWI-553 (2026-09-01) retired the `blockref`/`blocked_pending` mechanism but left\nfive Approved spine cells still *describing* it and shipped, calling them\n\"out-of-lane spine-hygiene for the owner.\" Review A rejected that: a stale\nApproved cell after a mechanism-removing diff is a **spec-vs-code contradiction**,\nnot out-of-lane prose — it is the DIRECT consequence of the diff and must be\nfixed in the same lane.\n\n**Why:** \"leave it for the owner / a later pass\" is the exact half-done pattern a\nCHANGES-REQUESTED round exists to catch. The mechanism's whole surface — LLR/TC\nprose AND its interface seam — travels with the removal.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- Re-point every Approved LLR/TC cell that names the deleted behaviour to the\n  new one. Editing the live cell (leave `status = \"Approved\"`) drifts it from\n  `docs/archive/last_approved/` → the drift IS the re-attest signal; the owner\n  blesses via the regenerated `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md` (`trace.py --approve\n  modified`). `Modified` status retired at D-9 step 7 — do not set it. See\n  [[d9-ladder-and-cell-attestation]].\n- Sweep the whole vocabulary, not just the reviewer's enumerated lines (they\n  missed a `TC-147` cell of the same class).\n- **Complete the interface consequence.** If the removed code was the ONLY\n  importer of a loader surface, its `IF-###` seam is now orphaned — retire it in\n  the same lane (interfaces carry no Retired status; all are `Drafted`, so\n  retirement = delete the row + its `Contract IF-###:` docstring in the owner\n  module + its `verifies` entry + any dangling pointer in sibling IF rationales).\n- **Never phrase the re-pointed reason with a `WI-###`/`OI-##` citation frame.**\n  `trace.py --strict-integrity`'s spine-stand-alone detector (process.md §3)\n  flags it as a provenance finding; state the system as standalone prose and put\n  the \"retired at WI-x\" account in `docs/log.d`. See\n  [[paraphrase-drift-causes-relitigation]].\n- Generated surfaces still naming the retired id (`interface-reference.md`,\n  `cli-reference.md`, `components.derived.toml`, trace `report.md`, `docs/stage`)\n  are left STALE on the work branch for the trunk regen — the commit hook SKIPs\n  their freshness `--check` on a work branch. But `test_derive_stage::\n  test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current` does NOT skip: editing a\n  fingerprinted spine input (`low-level-requirements.toml`, `test-cases.toml`)\n  reds it in the full suite — verify it's staleness (passed at HEAD~1) not\n  breakage, and do not hand-refresh `docs/stage`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3590,"cache_read_input_tokens":208433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3590},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2b0eee3-07f3-4ea6-8f78-0c8300a24eee","uuid":"6476f448-f22f-4194-a526-29fb002b5155","request_id":"req_011CecfcSSsxRghr7bY18okq"}
