asons with `WI-553/OI-70` citation frames — `trace.py --strict-integrity`'s spine-stand-alone detector flagged them, so I restated all five as standalone prose (provenance-findings 6→1, only pre-existing LLR-197 left). (2) The full suite shows 10 failures, **all accounted for, no regression**: 9 are the known pre-existing ruff-0.16 bootstrap-demo skew; 1 is expected `docs/stage` staleness from editing fingerprinted spine inputs (passed at HEAD~1; trunk regenerates it, never a work branch).\n\n**Verification:** commit-bar smoke green (1451 passed, within 60s budget); `check_trajectory --root .` exits 0; registry-integrity PASS. Three commits, each trailered `WI: WI-553`; tree clean. Generated surfaces still naming IF-138 left stale on-branch for trunk regen, as the WI already did for `interface-reference.md`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":522,"cache_read_input_tokens":215073,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":522},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2b0eee3-07f3-4ea6-8f78-0c8300a24eee","uuid":"78f56ba8-3b3f-43fb-9b8e-c3fb3e955186","request_id":"req_011Cecffeqbg4xBX69EjpRLJ"}
